","id":3756203009,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7f4xwB","user":{"login":"SartorialDragon","id":53511937,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNTExOTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53511937?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon","html_url":"https://github.com/SartorialDragon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SartorialDragon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T18:09:07Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T18:10:24Z","body":"I'm also on 4.5.1 stable and the problem persists. Enabling “Experimental Virtual Keyboard“ led to my keyboard showing, typing into the text edit works now (including backspace), BUT not saving the text input... my code for that is:\n\n`func _on_line_edit_text_changed(new_text: String) -> void:\nmyVariable = new_text`\n\nit works fine on PC and then displays the variable's content in a label on another page, but on mobile, the label just displays what was previously in the variable (the default name).\n\nAnyone got an idea what's going wrong? I assume the text input in the LineEdit doesn't get recognized as changed, despite showing new text.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3756203009/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5360440582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103387#issuecomment-5360440582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103387","id":5360440582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABP4HVBg","user":{"login":"agonzalez-qsi","id":44102830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MTAyODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44102830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi","html_url":"https://github.com/agonzalez-qsi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-20T19:04:34Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T19:04:34Z","body":"I can now confirm the regression gets introduced in the jump from 3.6beta5 to 3.6rc1.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5360440582/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5459092306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103387#issuecomment-5459092306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103387","id":5459092306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRWMjUg","user":{"login":"agonzalez-qsi","id":44102830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MTAyODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44102830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi","html_url":"https://github.com/agonzalez-qsi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agonzalez-qsi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-29T00:15:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-29T00:17:21Z","body":"The addition of IME implementation for Web exports (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/91610#issue-2280383933) is what causes the regression. Despite the backport of this feature from 4.x being mostly the same code, something about the way the engine calls `OS::set_ime_active` in 3.x is not equivalent to `DisplayServer::window_set_ime_active` in 4.x, and the IME div steals focus from the Input element. In Chrome on Android, no text ever gets captured. In Firefox on Android, additions are captured, but delete/backspace is not.\n\nYou can see this difference if you use Firefox's remote debugging feature to compare both major Godot versions, specifically 3.6+ and 4.5+ on non-C#. In both chosen editors, make a scene that is just a line edit in the center with a font that's at a sufficient readable size. Serve an HTML export of this scene on a network that can be accessed by the network device (needs to be served with HTTPS for 4.x to work, I used python 3.14+'s http_server with a dummy cert & key generated by openssl). \n\nIn 4.x, selecting the line edit causes the `<input>` to gain focus and 'display': 'block', and all keyboard input gets captured by the line edit. \n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"1079\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/168836d2-7513-4149-b9be-ae0663f58a2e\" />\n\nIn 3.x, selecting the line edit causes the `<div class=\"ime\">` to take focus after `<input>`, and only non-deleting keystrokes get captured.\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"1079\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b550d81-590a-4a56-8a12-f756d961e20d\" />\n\nFor a test, I decided to compile an export template for 3.6.2 where I commented out calls to `OS::get_singleton()->set_ime_active(true);` and `OS::get_singleton()->set_ime_position` from line_edit.cpp. This fixes the problem in Android Firefox and lets all keystrokes get captured, including delete/backspace. `<Input>` remains in focus and `<div class=\"ime\">` remains hidden. For obvious reasons, this is a non-viable solution, but does a good job at demonstrating the root problem.\n\n<img width=\"1918\" height=\"1079\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/263a9f53-d46c-45c5-b694-00a85eba0773\" />\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5459092306/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]